Modifications by su-engineering contributors include did:web credential
verification, OpenKYC login themes, deployment configuration, and the
independent package namespace, documentation, and development tooling.
Modified source files retain their original copyright notices.

The provider bundles didwebvh-core 0.3.1 from decentralized-identity/didwebvh-java
(Apache License 2.0), and java-json-canonicalization 1.1 by Anders Rundgren and
Samuel Erdtman (Apache License 2.0):
https://github.com/decentralized-identity/didwebvh-java
https://github.com/erdtman/java-json-canonicalization
The upstream Base58Btc facade is replaced with this project's Apache-2.0 adapter;
the upstream NovaCrypto Base58 dependency is excluded and is not distributed.
WebVH test vectors are copied from the Apache-2.0 didwebvh-test-suite via the
didwebvh-java repository. Provenance is recorded with the test fixtures.

